+# Integration Guide: Getting Records to All Users
+
+This library provides two complementary approaches to inject commit records into your development workflow. **Use both** to ensure full team coverage.
+
+## Approach 1: Hook-Based Injection (For Editors with Plugin Support)
+
+**Who this works for:** VS Code, JetBrains IDEs, and other editors with pre-tool-use hook APIs.
+
+**How it works:** When a file is about to be read, the hook fires and injects relevant records for that specific file.
+
+**Integration:**
+```typescript
+import { onPreToolUse } from "commitlore/src/index.ts";
+
+// In your editor's pre-tool-use hook:
+const context = onPreToolUse(repoPath, filePath);
+if (context) {
+  systemPrompt += "\n" + context;
+}
+```
+
+**Pros:**
+- Targeted injection: only records for files actually being touched
+- Works retroactively for files opened mid-session
+- Minimal system prompt bloat
+
+**Cons:**
+- Requires editor plugin support
+- Doesn't help users without hooks
+
+---
+
+## Approach 2: Bootstrap Injection (Universal Fallback)
+
+**Who this works for:** Teams using generic agents, CLI-only editors, cloud IDEs, or any environment without hook support.
+
+**How it works:** Load records for the entire repository (or key source paths) upfront before any tool use, injecting them into the initial system prompt.
+
+**Integration:**
+```typescript
+import { bootstrapForRepo } from "commitlore/src/index.ts";
+
+// At agent initialization (before any tool calls):
+const records = bootstrapForRepo(repoPath);
+if (records) {
+  systemPrompt = records + "\n\n" + systemPrompt;
+}
+```
+
+**Or with custom paths:**
+```typescript
+import { bootstrapRecords } from "commitlore/src/index.ts";
+
+const records = bootstrapRecords({
+  repo: repoPath,
+  paths: ["src/", "lib/", "api/"], // Your key directories
+});
+if (records) {
+  systemPrompt = records + "\n\n" + systemPrompt;
+}
+```
+
+**Pros:**
+- Works everywhere: no plugins, no hooks required
+- Eliminates "no records ever" for hook-less users
+- Simple one-time integration
+
+**Cons:**
+- Records for all paths at once, not per-file
+- Records are static for the session (don't update as files are accessed)
+- May add more context than needed
+
+---
+
+## Recommended Deployment
+
+1. **Add hook-based injection** for users with plugins (VS Code extension, JetBrains plugin).
+2. **Add bootstrap injection** to your agent's initialization as a **universal fallback**.
+
+This ensures:
+- ✅ Hook users get optimal per-file targeting
+- ✅ Hook-less users get *something* instead of nothing
+- ✅ Full team coverage, no blind spots
+
+### Example: Agent Initialization
+```typescript
+import { bootstrapForRepo } from "commitlore/src/index.ts";
+
+export async function initializeAgent(repoPath: string) {
+  let systemPrompt = "You are a helpful coding assistant.";
+  
+  // Universal: bootstrap records for all users
+  const records = bootstrapForRepo(repoPath);
+  if (records) {
+    systemPrompt = records + "\n\n" + systemPrompt;
+  }
+  
+  return createAgent({ systemPrompt });
+}
+```
+
+### Example: Editor Hook (Complements Bootstrap)
+```typescript
+import { onPreToolUse } from "commitlore/src/index.ts";
+
+export function onPreToolUse(repoPath: string, filePath: string) {
+  // Specific: inject records just for this file
+  // (augments or overrides the bootstrap context)
+  const fileRecords = onPreToolUse(repoPath, filePath);
+  if (fileRecords) {
+    return fileRecords;
+  }
+}
+```
+
+---
+
+## Deduplication
+
+Both approaches use the same underlying `recordsForPath()` query. The bootstrap loader automatically deduplicates records by `file:line` to avoid double-injection if both approaches are active.
+
+If a path appears in both hook-injected context and bootstrap context, the hook version takes precedence (it's fresher, file-specific).
